      "<strong>v1.8 &mdash; Stripe webhook handler (closes Phase B-full, the production-reliability backstop).</strong> Phase B-lite shipped in v1.7.2 closed the synchronous card-on-file path: <code>finalizeInvoice</code> &rarr; <code>pay()</code> returns &lsquo;paid&rsquo; in the same call, DB row gets stamped. That covers the happy path. Phase B-full closes the async paths: delayed-confirmation methods (SEPA / ACH / 3DS-required cards) settle hours-to-days later via webhook only; hard payment failures fire <code>invoice.payment_failed</code>; rare upstream Stripe issues fire <code>invoice.finalization_failed</code>. None of these mutate the DB without a webhook listener. v1.8 wires one. <strong>New route</strong>: <code>src/routes/api.webhooks.stripe.ts</code> &rarr; <code>POST /api/webhooks/stripe</code>. Pattern mirrors the existing <code>api.webhooks.scheduler.acuity.$secret.ts</code> handler: raw body read first (HMAC requires exact bytes), signature verified via <code>stripe.webhooks.constructEventAsync</code> (the Web-Crypto variant &mdash; CF Workers don&rsquo;t expose Node&rsquo;s <code>crypto.createHmac</code> sync API), audit row inserted into the pre-existing <code>stripe_webhook_events</code> table (unique on <code>stripe_event_id</code> &mdash; duplicate retries hit Postgres 23505 and return 200 immediately), then routed to the appropriate handler. <strong>Three handlers</strong>: (1) <code>invoice.paid</code> &rarr; <code>refill_invoices.status = &lsquo;paid&rsquo;</code>, <code>paid_at = now()</code>, <code>sent_at = now()</code> if still null. Belt-and-braces idempotency via <code>.is(&quot;paid_at&quot;, null)</code> guard on the update so late-arriving retries can&rsquo;t double-stamp. (2) <code>invoice.payment_failed</code> &rarr; status &lsquo;failed&rsquo;, with an &lsquo;already paid&rsquo; edge-case skip so a stale failure event arriving after a retry&rsquo;s success can&rsquo;t flip a paid row backward. (3) <code>invoice.finalization_failed</code> &rarr; same as payment_failed. <strong>Product gating</strong>: events without <code>metadata.product == &quot;refill&quot;</code> get audited but skip the refill_invoices update &mdash; this matches the contract our cron stamps on invoice creation in <code>generateMonthlyInvoiceForTenant</code>, and keeps the shared <code>stripe_webhook_events</code> table forensically complete without misclassifying legacy emma / WCS events. <strong>Always returns 200</strong> (even on handler errors) so Stripe doesn&rsquo;t exponential-retry-hammer the endpoint &mdash; failures are captured in the audit row&rsquo;s <code>error_message</code> column for replay. The only 4xx is missing signature header (legitimate bad request); the only 5xx is missing env (intentional &mdash; if env is broken we WANT Stripe to retry once it&rsquo;s fixed). <strong>Wiring</strong>: webhook secret lives at <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code> in CF Worker secrets (set via <code>wrangler secret put</code>). Endpoint URL <code>https://getrefill.app/api/webhooks/stripe</code> needs to be registered in Stripe Dashboard at <code>https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/webhooks/create</code> with events <code>invoice.paid</code>, <code>invoice.payment_failed</code>, <code>invoice.finalization_failed</code>. Once the secret is bound + the endpoint is live, the entire Phase B loop is webhook-backed. Touched: <code>src/routes/api.webhooks.stripe.ts</code> (new, 230 lines), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
